brand: Ride
model name: Warpig
model year: 2027
AUD price: $949.99
status: Preorder
estimated availability: May 1, 2026
available sizes: X-Small 142cm, Small 148cm, Medium 151cm, Large 154cm, X-Large 158cm
board type: All Mountain
flex: Mid
rider level: Intermediate
shape: Tapered Directional
camber type: Directional Zero Camber (flat zone underfoot with extended rocker in nose and tail)
width: Standard
sidecut type: Tapered Bi-Radial Sidecut (underfoot width of wide board while maintaining tip/tail width, enhances leverage on landings, improves grip through turns, stability on flat base)
mounting pattern: 2x4 Inserts
topsheet: Topless Topsheet (graphics transferred directly to fiberglass, enhances durability, reduces weight, minimises raw material usage)
laminate: Hybrid Glass (triaxial fiberglass on top, biaxial on base for balanced torsional flex and stiffness)
laminate reinforcement: Carbon Array 3 (three carbon stringers in binding zone collecting input from any stance width and pressure angles, directing rider input to opposite contact point)
laminate impact protection: Double Impact Plates (two layer urethane weaves beneath each binding area for compressive strength, preventing board breaks)
core: Performance Core (blend of high-strength Aspen and Bamboo wood for ideal balance of strength)
sidewall: Slim Walls (fully 3-D composite structure over Slimewall material, enhances energy transfer efficiency, reduces weight, boosts durability, improves damping)
base: Sintered, Stone Ground (heating and compressing polyethylene particles, porous structure absorbs wax efficiently, premium 4000 PTEX material)
edges: Cleave Edge Steel (nearly 50% more steel, unparalleled resistance to cracking, can be detuned to larger radii)
construction feature - Thin Con: Tapered tips and tails reducing swing weight, improving tip flex, and boosting durability
resin: Bio Resin (plant-based epoxy from renewable resources like vegetable oils, reduced carbon footprint)
sizing note: Shorter wider construction meant to be sized down shorter than regular all mountain board
terrain: Powder, Park, Groomers
